        <mxCell id="leg" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#D6DAE3;fontColor=#1B2A4A;fontSize=13;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;arcSize=7;" value="&lt;b&gt;Legend and rules&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size:11px&quot; color=&quot;#3a4a66&quot;&gt;Solid border: exists today. Dashed blue border: needed. Grey box: repository-local, or a tool that is not yet a skill. Solid arrow: hard dependency, the skill stops without it. Dashed arrow: reads, or composes.&lt;br&gt;1. A bundle depends only on bundles in the layers below it, and never on a repository above it. 2. A skill carries its method and its standards; where artefacts live is the repository&#39;s to declare. 3. The catalogue layer owns the definitions, the continuum; method bundles do not redefine them. 4. The scaffolding layer holds no layout of its own: it takes the house profile from the exemplar. 5. A solution keeps its architecture in a repository of its own (style A) or under docs/ of its own repository (style B); either way it is expressed with the continuum and checked by reconcile.&lt;/font&gt;" vertex="1">
